# Beyond &quot;Drill and Practice&quot; Programs.

**Authors:** Gravander, Jerry W.

## Abstract
Discusses applications of microcomputers to: (1) presentation of the content of humanities courses, especially computer assisted instruction and simulation programs; and (2) science, technology and society courses to reinforce points about limitations and appropriate uses of computers. Examples of computer programs used to facilitate these applications are appended. (MBR)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ327034

